Revision history for Langertha-Raider

{{$NEXT}}

    - Langertha-Raider is the merge of the App-Raider distribution with the
      agent engine extracted from Langertha core. Langertha::Raider,
      Langertha::Raider::Result and the Langertha::Raid orchestration layer
      (Raid::Loop, Raid::Parallel, Raid::Sequential) ship here under their
      own names; Langertha::Raider::Result is self-contained, and MCP
      tools go through Net::Async::MCP 0.004 or higher. Every
      App::Raider::* module is renamed to Langertha::Raider::*, with the CLI
      entry point App::Raider becoming Langertha::Raider::CLI; the raider and
      raider-hall executables keep their names. Requires Langertha 0.503.
    - The six App::Raider packages previously indexed on CPAN (App::Raider,
      App::Raider::FileTools, App::Raider::Plugin::Situation,
      App::Raider::Plugin::Trace, App::Raider::Skill, App::Raider::WebTools)
      ship as empty reserved-namespace stubs pointing to their
      Langertha::Raider replacements.
    - Fix filesystem confinement to reject symlink escapes for read and
      write operations, with regression tests.
    - Fix WebTools sync wrappers to await IO::Async futures through the
      loop, with injectable HTTP/search test doubles.
    - Hall Telegram access is fail-closed: an empty or missing allowlist
      rejects every message, allowlist holds sender user ids (from.id),
      and group chats must also be listed in the new allowed_chats.
      Rejections emit telegram.rejected; startup warns about empty
      allowlists and chat ids found in allowlist.
    - Fix Telegram replies: a raider spawned for a Telegram message gets
      its bot and chat id (RAIDER_HALL_TELEGRAM_BOT/_CHAT_ID), and
      telegram_reply is bound to that chat, needing only text.
    - Fix raider hall start/spawn/attach/logs/kill treating options as
      positional arguments (e.g. `start --daemon DIR` ignored DIR).
    - raider hall spawn/attach/logs/kill take an optional hall DIR as
      first argument without it leaking into NAME, MISSION or ID; a name
      that is a plain directory stays a name.
    - raider hall logs --follow prints new log output until the raider
      exits.
    - telegram.in events carry the sender's first_name and username, also
      in group chats.
    - Document that engine: is optional for hall raiders, and the hall
      MCP adapter (.raider-hall.mcp) as not implemented.
    - Fix plugin self-tools being offered to the model twice per raid.
    - Fix perl tools: perl_eval and perl_check run the current perl in the
      working root with the private lib; perl_check says BEGIN/use run;
      real errors are no longer reported as "timeout"; perl_cpanm rejects
      targets outside the root.
    - Explicit -m and -k beat model:/api_key: from .raider.yml, and the
      banner shows the model the engine is actually built with.
    - /reload and /pack keep a mission given with -M.
    - New raider config explain [options] and REPL /config: every
      effective setting with its source (flag, .raider.yml layer,
      environment, default).
    - perl_eval, perl_check and perl_cpanm kill the child process when it
      times out, and every timeout (including the retry after an
      auto-install and cpanm itself) comes back as a result instead of an
      exception; new install_timeout option. A relative
      preferred_lib_target resolves against the working root for PERL5LIB
      and cpanm alike.
    - raider hall start/stop/status/ps/install fail with "Not a
      directory" when DIR is not a directory instead of using the current
      directory.
    - MCP servers are named raider-files, raider-web, raider-perl and
      raider-hall; the Claude skill export is named raider
      (.claude/skills/raider/SKILL.md) and points out a leftover
      app-raider skill.
    - -o with raider's own keys (perl, packs=a,b, skills=a,b,
      preferred_lib_target, engine) configures raider like .raider.yml
      and overrides it; only engine attributes reach the engine.
    - bin/raider is a thin wrapper around internal
      Langertha::Raider::CLI::* classes (Main, REPL, Runner, Commands,
      PromptBuilder, Output). raider exits 0 on success, 1 when the run
      failed, 2 on a usage error and 3 on a configuration error; hall
      raider.done events report exit_code 1 for failed runs.
    - --json encodes UTF-8 once and keeps the live trace off unless
      --trace is given; raider -i reads piped input to its end.
    - /reload, the banner and the generated raider skill name a -M
      mission as the persona; the generated skill lists /config, /model,
      /packs and /pack.
    - Packs can activate by workspace detection (ADR 0012): declarative
      must / may / must_not rules on files and their content, from a
      pack's pack.yml or detect: in .raider.yml; switched off with
      no_detect:, detect: false, --no-pack NAME or --no-detect.
    - New bundled perl pack: in a Perl workspace (cpanfile, dist.ini,
      Makefile.PL or lib/**/*.pm) the perl_eval / perl_check / perl_cpanm
      tools are on without --perl; perl: false keeps them off.
    - raider config explain and /packs show each pack's source (flag,
      config, default, detected) and the rule clause that matched;
      /reload detects packs again. config explain also says whether the
      Perl tools are on and why (--perl, perl:, or the pack that asks for
      them). A pack directory without a SKILL.md loads.
    - Fix Hall singleton queue replay, --pack propagation, Telegram
      future retention, and MCP tool result handling.
    - Add `--pack NAME` CLI parsing for one-shot pack activation.
    - .raider.yml has one reader and writer, Langertha::Raider::Config
      (internal). Top-level keys apply next to default: and engine
      sections, so /model or a skills: hash no longer drops packs, perl
      or engine options; skills: merge across sections and with --claude
      / --openai / --skills, which all persist; engine: picks the engine;
      a file that does not parse, or a mapping under one of raider's own
      keys (packs:, perl:, engine:, ...) at the top, in default: or in an
      engine section, stops raider with a one-line error instead of being
      ignored.
      Raider-only keys never reach the engine constructor.
    - Hall raiders without an engine: leave the choice to raider
      (.raider.yml, then API-key autodetection) instead of anthropic.
    - Fix PerlTools local::lib cpanm invocation and record only
      successful installs.
    - Add .codex to .gitignore and .dockerignore as a Codex runtime
      mount marker.
    - Rework Docker builds to install from the Dist::Zilla build
      directory via cpm and the MetaCPAN resolver; no cpanfile.snapshot
      is shipped any more.
    - Move GitHub/Docker release publishing into maint/release-after.pl
      so run_after_release does not depend on shell redirection or
      conditionals.
    - Update README and POD for pack, PerlTools, Docker dist-dir build,
      Hall/ACP subcommands, and API-key-only Anthropic authentication.

    - Slice 1 — Perl-native tools: --perl unlocks perl_eval /
      perl_check / perl_cpanm, a private local::lib per raider, and
      auto-recovery on missing modules.
    - Slice 2 — Packs: toggleable persona/power bundles under
      share/packs/ (caveman/polite/teacher + git-guru/testing-fu/
      perl-hacker); /packs + /pack on|off|NAME slash commands.
    - Slice 3 — raider-hall daemon. `raider hall init` / `add-raider`
      / `start` / `ps` / `spawn` / `attach` / `kill` / `logs`. JSONL
      event bus + command protocol over a unix socket. 1name
      singleton queues persisted across restarts. longhouse-or-per-
      raider local::lib targets.
    - Slice 4 — Hall extras: non-blocking Schedule::Cron integration
      (IO::Async::Timer::Absolute + get_next_execution_time, opt-in
      coalesce); multi-bot Telegram long-poll via Net::Async::HTTP
      (the previous GET_form/POST_form calls didn't exist); MCP tool
      catalog on .raider-hall.mcp; systemd --user unit via
      `raider hall install`.
    - Slice 5 — ACP adapter: App::Raider::Hall::ACP speaks JSON-RPC
      2.0 line-framed over TCP (initialize / session/new /
      session/prompt / session/cancel). Configure via
      `acp: { port, host }` in .raider-hall.yml or `--acp-port N` on
      `raider hall start`.
    - ACP client: `raider acp ping|prompt|connect HOST:PORT` drives
      any ACP-conforming agent from the same binary. Under the hood:
      App::Raider::ACP::Client (blocking JSON-RPC 2.0).
    - Hall-side raider tools: telegram_reply / hall_status /
      hall_spawn are auto-exposed to raiders spawned under a hall
      (keyed on $RAIDER_HALL_SOCKET).
    - Docker-aware systemd install: inside a container, the unit is
      written to `.raider-hall/systemd/<name>.service` (the bind-mount
      surfaces it on the host), with a `cp` one-liner printed so the
      user just copies into ~/.config/systemd/user/. `--docker`
      template uses `docker run --rm -v $PWD:/work -e API_KEY…` and
      publishes the ACP port with `-p`.
    - Hall daemon fixes: double-$^X exec wrapper removed, mission
      passes as a single argv (not split on whitespace), Schedule::Cron
      no longer blocks the IO::Async loop, CHLD watcher removed (was
      double-reaping with IO::Async::Process). Shutdown grace-period
      timer is now actually started (was never firing).
    - App::Raider.packs attribute retyped from ArrayRef[Str] to
      App::Raider::Packs::Collection — the builder always returned a
      Collection and every hall-spawned raider died with a Moose
      type-constraint error the moment it built its mission.
    - Tests: t/20_packs.t, t/20_perltools.t, t/30_hall.t, t/40_acp.t
      (server dispatch), t/41_acp_client.t (forked hall, real
      client/server over TCP), t/42_acp_live.t (forked hall + real
      OpenAI API; gated on $OPENAI_API_KEY, 2–8s per run).
    - examples/multi-raider-hall/ walkthrough showing a minimal
      multi-raider village wired for cron + ACP.

0.003     2026-04-21 01:46:09Z

    - Switch bash tool from the retired MCP::Server::Run::Bash to
      MCP::Run::Bash (same API, renamed upstream distribution).
    - Dockerfile installs App::Raider from the dzil-built tarball
      instead of the source tree (no Makefile.PL in Dist::Zilla dists).
    - Docker Hub image published as raudssus/raider. dzil release now
      runs run_after_release hooks that create the GitHub release,
      build the runtime-root image, and push raudssus/raider:VERSION
      plus :latest.
    - Ship a cpanfile.snapshot for reproducible Carton deployments.

0.002     2026-04-20 20:28:50Z

    - /model REPL command: show current engine and model, list available
      models from the engine grouped by date-snapshot families (e.g.
      gpt-4o [+3 snapshots]); /model list [FILTER] for the full or
      substring-filtered list; /model NAME saves the chosen model to
      .raider.yml under default.model.
    - Model list colours: names in bright-blue, structural labels grey —
      consistent with the rest of the banner.
    - Fixed _build_skill_sources calling _normalize_skill_spec in scalar
      context, silently dropping the CLAUDE.md spec from the claude
      profile when loaded from .raider.yml ("seeing CLAUDE.md, ignoring"
      even with profiles: claude active).
    - Fixed Term::ReadLine::Gnu detection: require Term::ReadLine::Gnu
      fails with "invalid to load directly"; now detected via
      Term::ReadLine->new + ->ReadLine =~ /Gnu/.
    - Readline history now persists across Ctrl-C / SIGTERM via signal
      handlers that call WriteHistory before exit.

0.001     2026-04-20 17:44:05Z

    - Initial release.
    - CLI agent (App::Raider) wrapping Langertha::Raider with a default
      viking persona ("Langertha"), caveman-style communication, and
      effectively unlimited tool-calling iterations per raid.
    - Tools: filesystem (list_files, read_file, write_file, edit_file),
      bash (MCP::Server::Run::Bash), web_search and web_fetch
      (Net::Async::WebSearch + Net::Async::HTTP).
    - Engine auto-detection from available *_API_KEY env var with cheap
      per-engine default models (claude-haiku-4-5, gpt-4o-mini, etc.).
    - .raider.md for persona customization; hot-reload via /reload;
      /prompt spawns a sub-agent prompt-builder that writes .raider.md.
    - .raider.yml for engine options (temperature, response_size, ...)
      with flat or default/<engine> layers; -o key=value CLI override.
    - Skill / profile loading: --claude loads CLAUDE.md and
      .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md; --openai/--codex loads AGENTS.md;
      --skills DIR adds plain-markdown dirs. Choices persist to
      .raider.yml with (saved) banner tag on first use.
    - App::Raider::Skill generates self-describing how-to-use-raider
      documentation from the live config, as plain markdown or as a
      Claude Code SKILL.md with YAML frontmatter; usable via CLI
      (--export-skill / --export-claude-skill) or REPL (/skill,
      /skill-claude).
    - REPL: Term::ReadLine::Gnu with persistent ~/.raider_history,
      IO::Prompt::Tiny fallback; plain-ASCII output with blue/green
      palette; slash commands /help /clear /metrics /stats /reload
      /prompt /skill /skill-claude /quit.
    - App::Raider::Plugin::Trace streams per-iteration tool calls,
      args, results and cumulative token counts; meta-line after each
      raid shows elapsed time, history size vs. context cap, and
      cumulative tokens in / out / total.
    - App::Raider::Plugin::Situation injects a compact single-line
      situation block (local time, timezone, host, user) at the start
      of each session.
    - Auto-compression at 70% of a 40k-token context window to stay
      under typical per-minute rate limits.
    - Dockerfile with multi-stage build: runtime-root for root use,
      runtime-user with RAIDER_UID/RAIDER_GID build args for host-uid
      matching. README includes a shell-alias recipe that mounts $PWD
      and forwards API-key env vars.
